* device-pnp-array -- GENERATED by sim/tools/mk_klt_device_request.py, do not edit
.include "design.ngspice"
* tb_pnp_array.spice -- equal-total-emitter-current effective ratio of the
* four-unit Q2 realisation (DR-0007 Decision item 1, issue #208)
*
* Two grounded-base/collector diode-connected branches, each forced with the
* SAME total emitter current Ie (the Brokaw core enforces equal emitter
* currents in Q1 and Q2, not equal per-unit currents):
*
*   branch U  : ONE   pnp_05p00x05p00  carrying Ie           -> node eu
*   branch A  : FOUR  pnp_05p00x05p00 in parallel, together
*               carrying Ie (Ie/4 per unit by symmetry)       -> node ea
*   branch M  : ONE   pnp_10p00x10p00 carrying Ie (the pre-DR-0007
*               monolithic Q2; same-bench reference for lambda)  -> node em
*
* A_eff(array)      = exp((VBE_U - VBE_A) / VT),  VT = k(T+273.15)/q
* A_eff(monolithic) = exp((VBE_U - VBE_M) / VT)
*
* PNP subckt node order is (collector base emitter); collector and base are
* the grounded p-substrate, as in sim/device-pnp-vbe/testbench/tb_pnp_vbe.spice.
* Zero-volt sources Vbu/Vba/Vbm sense base current.
*
* Ie is swept as v(ctrl) = Ie in uA (4.00 .. 7.00 step 0.01, so the design
* point 5.07 uA and the historical 6.5 uA point are exact sweep points).
* No supply rail exists on this bench (supply axis = "nosupply").
*
* Fragment: no .include/.lib/.temp/.control/.end -- the `klt sim` request
* (sim/tools/mk_klt_device_request.py) supplies models, .temp and .meas.

Vctrl ctrl 0 dc 5.07

* ---- unit branch: one 5x5 carrying the full Ie ----
Bu    0 eu I = v(ctrl) * 1e-6
Vbu   bu 0 dc 0
XQu   0 bu eu pnp_05p00x05p00

* ---- array branch: four parallel 5x5 sharing the same total Ie ----
Ba    0 ea I = v(ctrl) * 1e-6
Vba   ba 0 dc 0
XQa0  0 ba ea pnp_05p00x05p00
XQa1  0 ba ea pnp_05p00x05p00
XQa2  0 ba ea pnp_05p00x05p00
XQa3  0 ba ea pnp_05p00x05p00

* ---- monolithic reference: one 10x10 carrying the full Ie ----
Bm    0 em I = v(ctrl) * 1e-6
Vbm   bm 0 dc 0
XQm   0 bm em pnp_10p00x10p00

